WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Dad wants us to pick up
where he left off --

00:00:00.694 --> 00:00:03.661
Saving people, hunting things,
the family business.

00:00:05.999 --> 00:00:08.966
You know the truth
about sammy.

00:00:08.999 --> 00:00:11.500
I've known for a while.

00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:14.699
You get premonitions
of people about to die?

00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:16.799
Death visions?

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:17.999
Yeah.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.467
Sam: the demon
said he had plans for me.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.966
Do you have any idea
what he meant by that?

00:00:22.999 --> 00:00:24.666
No.

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:27.699
I want you to watch out
for sammy, okay?

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:30.033
Did he say anything
to you?

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:32.033
No.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.899
I can't talk about this
to sammy.

00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:36.899
I've got to keep
my game face on.

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:39.567
You're erratic,
except for when you're hunting.

00:00:39.632 --> 00:00:41.366
'Cause then,
you're downright scary.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.699
The truth is,
i'm not handling it very well.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.866
You're tailspinning, man,
and you won't let me help you.

00:01:18.732 --> 00:01:21.433
No, no, no, no.
No, you're not gonna --

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.100
No, i swear!
It's not in me!

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.632
Oh, god.
We're all gonna die.

00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:28.100
Maybe he's telling
the truth.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.033
He's not him --
Not anymore.

00:01:30.066 --> 00:01:32.766
Stop it! Ask her!
Ask the doctor!

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:34.266
It's not in me!

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.866
I...just...

00:01:37.066 --> 00:01:38.433
i can't tell.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.899
No, please, don't.
Don't.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.632
I've got no choice.

00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:46.266
It's not in me.

00:02:07.699 --> 00:02:08.966
Sam?

00:02:11.978 --> 00:02:15.725
<Font color="#ffff00">www.1000fr.Com present</font>

00:02:15.725 --> 00:02:20.688
uploaded for opensubtitles.org by najic (",)

00:02:24.008 --> 00:02:26.731
<i>Woman:
continue on or-224 west.</i>

00:02:26.732 --> 00:02:29.233
There are only two towns
in the u.S. Named rivergrove.

00:02:29.266 --> 00:02:31.933
How come you're so sure
it's the one in oregon?

00:02:33.266 --> 00:02:36.366
There was a picture.

00:02:38.433 --> 00:02:40.066
Okay, what else?

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:45.266
I saw a dark room, some people,
and a guy tied to a chair.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.100
And i ventilated him?

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:50.833
Yeah. You thought there was
something inside him.

00:02:50.866 --> 00:02:54.397
A demon? Was he possessed?

00:02:54.397 --> 00:02:54.732
All your weirdo visions

00:02:54.766 --> 00:02:56.599
Are always tied to
the yellow-Eyed demon.

00:02:56.632 --> 00:02:59.400
Was there any black smoke?
Did we try to exorcise him?

00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:02.333
No. Nothing.
You just plugged him.

00:03:02.366 --> 00:03:03.333
That's it.

00:03:03.366 --> 00:03:05.100
Well, i'm sure
i had a good reason.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.100
I sure hope so.

00:03:09.386 --> 00:03:12.152
What does that mean?

00:03:13.385 --> 00:03:16.619
I'm not gonna
waste an innocent man.

00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:18.516
I wouldn't.
I never said you would.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:19.950
Fine.
Fine.

00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:21.583
Look, we don't
know what it is.

00:03:21.616 --> 00:03:24.284
But whatever it is, that guy
in the chair is a part of it.

00:03:24.316 --> 00:03:26.284
So, let's find him
and see what's what.

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:27.883
Fine.
Fine.

00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:12.850
He was there.

00:04:16.616 --> 00:04:17.583
Morning.

00:04:17.616 --> 00:04:19.883
Morning.
Can i help you?

00:04:19.917 --> 00:04:22.783
Yeah. Billy gibbons,
frank beard.

00:04:22.817 --> 00:04:24.217
U.S. Marshals.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.083
What's this about?

00:04:26.117 --> 00:04:27.117
We're looking for someone.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.950
A young man, early 20s.

00:04:29.983 --> 00:04:34.817
He'd have a thin scar
right below his hairline.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.750
What did he do?

00:04:36.783 --> 00:04:38.349
We're actually
looking for someone else,

00:04:38.383 --> 00:04:40.516
But we think
this young man can help us.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:43.217
He's not in any kind of trouble
or anything. Not yet.

00:04:46.983 --> 00:04:50.616
I think maybe you
know who he is, master sergeant.

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:53.783
My dad was in the corps.
He was a corporal.

00:04:53.817 --> 00:04:54.783
What company?

00:04:54.817 --> 00:04:56.117
Echo-2-1.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.550
So, can you help us?

00:05:00.316 --> 00:05:04.284
Duane tanner's
got a scar like that.

00:05:04.316 --> 00:05:06.050
But i know him.

00:05:06.083 --> 00:05:08.083
Good kid.
Keeps his nose clean.

00:05:08.117 --> 00:05:10.950
Oh, i'm sure he does.
Do you know where he lives?

00:05:10.983 --> 00:05:16.117
With his family,
up aspen way.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.117
Thank you.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.150
Thanks.

00:05:31.284 --> 00:05:33.150
Hey.

00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:42.316
"Croatoan"?

00:05:42.349 --> 00:05:43.449
Yeah.

00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:47.650
Roanoke. Lost colony.
Ring a bell?

00:05:47.683 --> 00:05:50.983
Dean, did you pay any attention
to history class?

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.950
Yeah. The shot heard
around the world.

00:05:53.983 --> 00:05:55.650
How bills become laws.

00:05:55.683 --> 00:05:59.083
That's not school.
That's "schoolhouse rock."

00:06:00.516 --> 00:06:01.483
Whatever.

00:06:01.516 --> 00:06:03.449
Roanoke was one
of the first

00:06:03.483 --> 00:06:06.184
English colonies in america --
Late 1500s.

00:06:06.217 --> 00:06:08.217
Oh, yeah, yeah,
i do remember that.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:10.050
The only thing
they left behind

00:06:10.083 --> 00:06:12.550
Was a single word carved
in a tree.

00:06:12.583 --> 00:06:13.817
"Croatoan."

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.783
Yeah, and there were
theories --

00:06:15.817 --> 00:06:16.883
Indian raid, disease --

00:06:16.917 --> 00:06:18.483
But nobody knows
what really happened.

00:06:18.516 --> 00:06:22.150
They were all just gone,
wiped out overnight.

00:06:22.184 --> 00:06:26.083
You don't think
that's what's going on here.

00:06:26.117 --> 00:06:28.550
Whatever i saw in my head,
it sure wasn't good.

00:06:31.017 --> 00:06:32.650
But what do you think
could do that?

00:06:36.516 --> 00:06:39.150
Well, i mean, like i said,
all your weirdo visions

00:06:39.184 --> 00:06:42.150
Are always tied to the
yellow-Eyed demon somehow, so...

00:06:42.184 --> 00:06:44.817
we should get help.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.050
Bobby. Ellen, maybe.

00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:49.117
Yeah,
that's a good idea.

00:06:54.117 --> 00:06:56.284
I don't have a signal.

00:07:02.117 --> 00:07:04.284
I don't either.

00:07:14.383 --> 00:07:17.683
The line's dead.

00:07:17.716 --> 00:07:19.349
I'll tell you one thing --

00:07:19.383 --> 00:07:21.250
If i was gonna
massacre a town,

00:07:21.284 --> 00:07:23.883
That'd be my first step.

00:07:41.483 --> 00:07:43.217
Yeah?

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:45.783
Hi, looking for duane tanner.
He lives here, right?

00:07:45.817 --> 00:07:48.050
He's my brother.

00:07:48.083 --> 00:07:49.650
Can we talk to him?

00:07:49.683 --> 00:07:51.750
He's not here right now.

00:07:51.783 --> 00:07:52.983
Do you know where he is?

00:07:53.017 --> 00:07:56.184
Yeah, he went on a fishing trip
up by roslyn lake.

00:07:56.217 --> 00:07:58.017
Your parents home?
Yeah, they're inside.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.050
Man:
jake, who is it?

00:08:00.683 --> 00:08:03.316
Dean:
hi, u.S. Marshals, sir.

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:05.983
We're looking
for your son duane.

00:08:06.017 --> 00:08:07.316
He's not in trouble,
is he?

00:08:07.349 --> 00:08:09.983
We just need to ask him
a couple routine questions.

00:08:10.017 --> 00:08:12.150
When is he due back
from his trip?

00:08:12.184 --> 00:08:13.716
I'm not sure.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:16.917
Well,
maybe your wife knows.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:19.416
No, i don't know.
She's not here right now.

00:08:19.449 --> 00:08:20.817
Well,
your son said she was.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:21.883
Did i?

00:08:21.917 --> 00:08:24.683
She's getting groceries.

00:08:24.716 --> 00:08:26.583
So, when duane gets back,

00:08:26.616 --> 00:08:28.817
There's a number
where he can get ahold of you?

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.150
Oh, no, we'll just check in
with you later.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:39.017
That was kind of creepy,
right?

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:40.349
A little too stepford?

00:08:40.383 --> 00:08:42.217
Big-Time.

00:08:52.483 --> 00:08:56.817
It's okay, mom.
It's not gonna hurt.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:18.483
Put it down!

00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:58.896
Hello?

00:09:58.929 --> 00:10:01.262
Hello?
We need a doctor here.

00:10:02.924 --> 00:10:04.725
Mrs. Tanner,
what happened?

00:10:04.758 --> 00:10:05.891
She's been attacked.

00:10:05.924 --> 00:10:06.924
Dr. Lee?

00:10:10.024 --> 00:10:10.991
It's okay.

00:10:11.024 --> 00:10:12.725
Bring her in.

00:10:12.758 --> 00:10:13.924
Okay.

00:10:15.857 --> 00:10:17.824
Hey.

00:10:17.857 --> 00:10:20.525
Is that...?

00:10:21.924 --> 00:10:23.325
Mr. Tanner?

00:10:23.358 --> 00:10:25.325
Was he attacked, too?

00:10:25.358 --> 00:10:27.625
Uh, no, actually,
he did the attacking,

00:10:27.658 --> 00:10:29.458
And then
he got himself shot.

00:10:29.491 --> 00:10:30.824
Shot?
Yeah.

00:10:30.857 --> 00:10:32.058
And who are you?

00:10:32.091 --> 00:10:35.224
U.S. Marshal.
I'd show you my badge, but...

00:10:35.258 --> 00:10:37.857
oh, sorry.
Bring him back here.

00:10:40.024 --> 00:10:42.158
Wait, you said jake
helped him?

00:10:42.191 --> 00:10:43.991
Your son jake?

00:10:44.024 --> 00:10:46.224
They beat me.

00:10:47.957 --> 00:10:49.891
Tied me up.

00:10:49.924 --> 00:10:52.857
I don't believe it.

00:10:52.891 --> 00:10:54.191
Pam.

00:10:54.224 --> 00:10:56.358
Beverly,
do you have any idea

00:10:56.391 --> 00:10:57.957
Why they would act
this way?

00:10:57.991 --> 00:10:59.891
Any history
of chemical dependency?

00:10:59.924 --> 00:11:02.224
No, of course not.

00:11:02.258 --> 00:11:04.191
I don't know why.

00:11:04.224 --> 00:11:08.891
One minute,
they were my husband and my son,

00:11:08.924 --> 00:11:13.258
And the next,
they had the devil in them.

00:11:15.957 --> 00:11:17.792
We've got to talk.

00:11:24.091 --> 00:11:26.124
Those guys were whacked
out of their gourds.

00:11:26.158 --> 00:11:28.024
What do you think,
mass possession?

00:11:28.058 --> 00:11:30.525
If it is a possession,
there could be more.

00:11:30.558 --> 00:11:31.692
God knows how many.

00:11:31.725 --> 00:11:33.792
It could be like
a freaking shriner convention.

00:11:33.824 --> 00:11:37.722
Of course, that's one way
to wipe out a town --

00:11:37.722 --> 00:11:38.425
You take it
from the inside.

00:11:38.458 --> 00:11:41.091
We didn't see any
of the demon smoke with tanner

00:11:41.124 --> 00:11:42.643
Or any
of the other usual signs.

00:11:42.643 --> 00:11:45.957
Something turned him
into a monster.

00:11:45.991 --> 00:11:48.898
You know, if you would have
taken out the other one,

00:11:48.898 --> 00:11:50.485
There would be one less
to worry about.

00:11:50.485 --> 00:11:52.672
I'm sorry.
I hesitated.

00:11:52.673 --> 00:11:53.740
It was a kid.

00:11:53.774 --> 00:11:55.006
No, it was an "it."

00:11:55.039 --> 00:11:58.640
It's not the best time
for a bleeding heart, sam.

00:11:58.673 --> 00:11:59.973
How's the patient?

00:12:00.006 --> 00:12:01.973
Terrible. What the hell
happened out there?

00:12:02.006 --> 00:12:03.973
You just killed
my next-Door neighbor.

00:12:04.006 --> 00:12:05.140
We didn't have a choice.

00:12:05.173 --> 00:12:08.056
Maybe so,
but we need the county sheriff.

00:12:08.056 --> 00:12:08.897
The phones are down.

00:12:08.897 --> 00:12:11.431
I know. I tried. Tell me
you've got a police radio.

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:14.398
Yeah, we do, but it crapped out
just like everything else.

00:12:14.431 --> 00:12:16.431
I don't understand
what is happening.

00:12:16.464 --> 00:12:17.598
How far is it
to the next town?

00:12:17.631 --> 00:12:19.564
It's about 40 miles down
to sidewinder.

00:12:19.598 --> 00:12:21.829
I'm gonna go down there
and see if i can find some help.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.630
My partner will stick around
and keep you guys safe.

00:12:24.663 --> 00:12:26.396
Safe from what?

00:12:28.463 --> 00:12:30.797
We'll get back to you
on that.

00:13:52.396 --> 00:13:54.730
Huh.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:57.964
What?

00:13:57.997 --> 00:14:01.129
His lymphocyte percentage
is pretty high.

00:14:01.163 --> 00:14:03.797
His body was fighting off
a viral infection.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:06.396
Really?
What kind of virus?

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.163
I can't say for sure.

00:14:08.196 --> 00:14:10.678
An infection could have made him
act like that?

00:14:10.679 --> 00:14:15.250
Some can cause dementia,
but not that kind of violence.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.584
And besides,

00:14:16.584 --> 00:14:18.562
I've never heard of one
that did this to the blood.

00:14:18.562 --> 00:14:19.482
Did what?

00:14:19.482 --> 00:14:21.329
There's
this weird residue.

00:14:22.215 --> 00:14:25.581
If i didn't know better,
i'd say it was sulfur.

00:14:32.148 --> 00:14:33.815
Sulfur.

00:15:07.714 --> 00:15:09.449
Oh, ho, ho. Hey.

00:15:09.482 --> 00:15:11.115
Sorry. Road's closed.

00:15:11.148 --> 00:15:13.282
Yeah, i can see that.
What's up?

00:15:13.315 --> 00:15:14.449
Quarantine.

00:15:14.482 --> 00:15:16.781
Quarantine?
What is it?

00:15:16.815 --> 00:15:18.115
Don't know.

00:15:18.148 --> 00:15:19.948
Something going around
out there.

00:15:19.981 --> 00:15:21.781
Uh-Huh.
Who told you that?

00:15:21.815 --> 00:15:23.115
County sheriff.

00:15:23.148 --> 00:15:24.581
Is he here?

00:15:24.614 --> 00:15:27.015
No. He called.

00:15:27.048 --> 00:15:28.714
Say, why don't
you get out of the car,

00:15:28.748 --> 00:15:30.115
And we'll talk a little?

00:15:30.148 --> 00:15:32.515
Well,
you are a handsome devil,

00:15:32.549 --> 00:15:35.082
But i don't swing that way,
sorry.

00:15:35.115 --> 00:15:37.315
I'd sure appreciate it
if you got out of the car,

00:15:37.348 --> 00:15:38.449
Just for a quick minute.

00:15:40.581 --> 00:15:42.714
Yeah, i bet you would.

00:15:44.781 --> 00:15:46.581
Stop!

00:15:46.614 --> 00:15:47.714
Stop!

00:16:01.681 --> 00:16:04.215
I don't understand.

00:16:04.248 --> 00:16:08.549
Are you saying my husband
and jake had a disease?

00:16:08.614 --> 00:16:10.781
That's what
we're trying to find out.

00:16:10.815 --> 00:16:14.781
Now, during the attack,
do you remember --

00:16:14.815 --> 00:16:18.648
Did you have any direct contact
with their blood?

00:16:18.681 --> 00:16:19.915
Oh, my god.

00:16:19.948 --> 00:16:23.282
You don't think
i've got this virus, do you?

00:16:23.315 --> 00:16:25.748
Beverly, i don't know
what to think,

00:16:25.781 --> 00:16:29.115
But with your permission,
we'll take a blood sample.

00:16:38.981 --> 00:16:40.082
Aah!

00:16:40.848 --> 00:16:41.981
Aah!

00:16:47.148 --> 00:16:48.482
Aah!

00:17:01.082 --> 00:17:02.382
Hands where
i can see them!

00:17:02.415 --> 00:17:03.714
Son of a --

00:17:03.748 --> 00:17:05.614
Get out of the car!

00:17:06.981 --> 00:17:08.182
Out of the car!

00:17:08.215 --> 00:17:10.681
Crap.

00:17:10.714 --> 00:17:12.781
All right.
Easy there, big guy.

00:17:16.781 --> 00:17:18.082
Put it down!
Lower it now!

00:17:18.115 --> 00:17:19.082
Are you one of them?!

00:17:19.115 --> 00:17:20.082
No, are you?!
No!

00:17:20.115 --> 00:17:22.581
You could be lying!
So could you!

00:17:22.614 --> 00:17:24.714
We could do this all day.
All right.

00:17:24.748 --> 00:17:27.515
Let's just take it easy
before we kill each other.

00:17:29.681 --> 00:17:31.648
What's going on
with everybody?

00:17:31.681 --> 00:17:33.648
I don't know.

00:17:33.681 --> 00:17:35.748
My neighbor, mr. Rogers --

00:17:35.781 --> 00:17:37.748
You've got a neighbor
named mr. Rogers?

00:17:37.781 --> 00:17:38.981
Not anymore.

00:17:39.015 --> 00:17:42.981
He came at me with a hatchet.
I put him down.

00:17:43.015 --> 00:17:44.482
He's not the only one.

00:17:44.515 --> 00:17:46.915
I mean, it's happening
to everyone.

00:17:46.948 --> 00:17:48.082
I'm heading to doc's place.

00:17:48.115 --> 00:17:49.581
There's still
some people left.

00:17:49.614 --> 00:17:50.781
I'm getting the hell out.

00:17:50.815 --> 00:17:52.948
There's no way out.
They got the bridge covered.

00:17:52.981 --> 00:17:55.415
I don't believe you.
Fine, stay here.
Be my guest.

00:18:11.948 --> 00:18:14.781
Well, this ought to be
a relaxing drive.

00:18:21.148 --> 00:18:23.815
What if we all have it?

00:18:23.848 --> 00:18:26.648
What if we all go crazy?

00:18:26.681 --> 00:18:28.781
You've got to stay calm.
All we can do is wait.

00:18:28.815 --> 00:18:30.282
The marshal
is bringing help.

00:18:30.315 --> 00:18:33.382
I can't.
I've got to go.

00:18:33.415 --> 00:18:34.714
Pam?

00:18:34.748 --> 00:18:37.648
No, you don't understand.
My boyfriend's out there.

00:18:37.681 --> 00:18:39.282
I've got to make sure
he's okay.

00:18:42.581 --> 00:18:46.881
Hey, hey, hey, wait.
Wait, please.

00:18:46.915 --> 00:18:49.915
Look, i know you're upset,
all right.

00:18:49.948 --> 00:18:51.948
But it's safer
if you stay here for now.

00:18:51.981 --> 00:18:53.948
Help is coming.

00:18:58.282 --> 00:19:00.614
There they are.

00:19:02.065 --> 00:19:04.044
??

00:19:10.549 --> 00:19:13.515
Did you guys
get to a phone?

00:19:13.549 --> 00:19:14.848
Roadblock.

00:19:14.881 --> 00:19:16.515
I'm gonna have a word.
Doc's inside.

00:19:16.549 --> 00:19:18.881
All right.

00:19:18.915 --> 00:19:20.581
What's going on
out there, dean?

00:19:20.614 --> 00:19:22.680
I feel like chuck heston
in "the omega man."

00:19:22.681 --> 00:19:25.609
Sarge is the only sane person
i could find.

00:19:25.609 --> 00:19:27.350
What are we dealing with?
Do you know?

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:28.650
Yeah,
doc thinks it's a virus.

00:19:28.683 --> 00:19:30.849
Okay, great.
What do you think?

00:19:30.882 --> 00:19:32.216
I think she's right.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.782
And i think the infected

00:19:33.816 --> 00:19:36.037
Are trying to infect others
with blood-To-Blood contact.

00:19:36.037 --> 00:19:39.369
The virus leaves traces
of sulfur in the blood.

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:43.134
A demonic virus?
More like demonic
germ warfare.

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:46.188
At least it explains
why i've been having visions.

00:19:47.233 --> 00:19:48.813
It's like
a biblical plague.

00:19:48.813 --> 00:19:51.947
Yeah. You don't know
how right you are, dean.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:54.281
I've been pouring
through dad's journal.

00:19:54.314 --> 00:19:56.780
I found something
about the roanoke colony.

00:19:56.813 --> 00:19:59.314
Dad always had a theory
about "croatoan."

00:19:59.347 --> 00:20:00.947
He thought
it was a demon's name --

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:02.648
Sometimes known as daeva
or reshef --

00:20:02.713 --> 00:20:05.147
A demon of plague
and pestilence.

00:20:05.181 --> 00:20:08.080
Well, that's terrific.
Why here? Why now?

00:20:08.114 --> 00:20:09.414
I have no idea.

00:20:10.481 --> 00:20:13.947
But, dean, who knows
how far this thing can spread?

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.181
We've got to get out of here.
We've got to warn people.

00:20:16.214 --> 00:20:18.281
Mark: they've got one.
In here.

00:20:20.614 --> 00:20:21.747
What do you mean?

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:23.281
The wife --
She's infected.

00:20:23.314 --> 00:20:25.014
We've got to take care
of this.

00:20:25.047 --> 00:20:26.680
We can't just leave her
in there.

00:20:26.713 --> 00:20:28.514
My neighbors --
They were strong.

00:20:28.548 --> 00:20:30.813
The longer we wait,
the stronger she'll get.

00:20:37.247 --> 00:20:39.214
You're gonna kill
beverly tanner?

00:20:39.247 --> 00:20:41.614
Doctor, could there
be any treatment?

00:20:41.648 --> 00:20:43.780
Some kind of cure
for this?

00:20:46.014 --> 00:20:47.514
Can you cure it?

00:20:47.548 --> 00:20:49.181
I don't even know
what "it" is.

00:20:49.214 --> 00:20:52.181
It's a matter of time
before she breaks through.

00:20:52.214 --> 00:20:54.014
You can't shoot her
like an animal.

00:20:54.047 --> 00:20:56.614
Sam.

00:21:14.247 --> 00:21:17.980
Mark.
What are you doing?

00:21:18.014 --> 00:21:21.414
Mark, it's them.

00:21:21.447 --> 00:21:24.847
They locked me in here.
They tried to kill me.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:26.980
They're infected,
not me.

00:21:27.014 --> 00:21:29.914
Please, mark.

00:21:29.947 --> 00:21:32.481
You've known me
all your life.

00:21:32.514 --> 00:21:35.680
Please.

00:21:35.713 --> 00:21:38.047
Are you sure
she's one of them?

00:21:39.713 --> 00:21:41.548
Yeah.

00:22:33.566 --> 00:22:35.867
Oh, god! Is there any on me?!
Am i okay?!

00:22:35.900 --> 00:22:37.167
You're clean.
You're okay.

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:40.600
Why are we staying here?
Please, let's just go.

00:22:40.633 --> 00:22:42.767
We can't, 'cause those things
are everywhere.

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:44.200
Oh, god.
Why is this happening?

00:22:44.234 --> 00:22:47.033
Shh, shh, shh.

00:22:49.833 --> 00:22:53.200
She's right about one thing.
We can't stay here.

00:22:53.234 --> 00:22:55.633
We've got to get out of here,
get to the roadhouse,

00:22:55.666 --> 00:22:57.200
Let people know
what's coming.

00:22:57.234 --> 00:22:58.533
That's a good point.

00:22:58.566 --> 00:23:00.666
"Night of the living dead"
didn't exactly end pretty.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:04.067
Lots of folks
up here are good with rifles.

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:06.900
Even with all your hardware,
we're easy targets.

00:23:06.933 --> 00:23:11.033
So, unless you've got
some explosives...

00:23:15.566 --> 00:23:17.466
we could make some.

00:23:22.733 --> 00:23:25.000
Duane:
let me in, please!

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:28.433
It's duane tanner.

00:23:32.100 --> 00:23:33.733
Oh, thank god.

00:23:39.700 --> 00:23:42.000
Duane, you okay?

00:23:42.033 --> 00:23:45.000
That's the guy that i...

00:23:45.033 --> 00:23:46.333
yeah.

00:23:46.366 --> 00:23:47.600
Who else is in here?

00:23:47.633 --> 00:23:50.100
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Easy there, chief.

00:23:50.134 --> 00:23:53.533
Hey, doc, give duane
a good once-Over, would you?

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:58.000
Pam?

00:23:58.033 --> 00:23:59.167
Who are you?

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:01.566
Never mind who i am.
Doc.

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:03.900
Yeah, okay.

00:24:03.933 --> 00:24:05.466
Duane, where you been?

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.633
I was on a fishing trip
up by roslyn.

00:24:07.666 --> 00:24:09.299
I came back
this afternoon.

00:24:09.333 --> 00:24:11.967
I saw roger mcgill being dragged
out of his house

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:13.700
By people we know.

00:24:13.733 --> 00:24:16.134
They started cutting him
with knives.

00:24:16.167 --> 00:24:19.100
I ran. I've been hiding
in the woods ever since.

00:24:19.134 --> 00:24:20.733
Has anybody
seen my mom and dad?

00:24:20.767 --> 00:24:23.933
Awkward.

00:24:25.600 --> 00:24:28.399
You're bleeding.

00:24:30.333 --> 00:24:31.900
Where did you get that?

00:24:31.933 --> 00:24:33.633
I was running.
I must have tripped.

00:24:33.666 --> 00:24:36.900
Tie him up.
There's rope in there.

00:24:36.933 --> 00:24:38.500
Wait --
Sit down!

00:24:39.767 --> 00:24:42.666
Sorry, duane. He's right.
We've got to be careful.

00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:44.867
Careful? About what?

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:46.167
Did they bleed on you?

00:24:46.200 --> 00:24:47.666
No.
What the hell?! No!

00:24:47.700 --> 00:24:50.666
Doc, any way to know for sure?
Any test?

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:52.747
I've studied beverly's blood
work backwards and forwards.

00:24:52.747 --> 00:24:54.698
??

00:24:54.698 --> 00:24:57.199
It took three hours
for the virus to incubate.

00:24:57.199 --> 00:24:59.232
Sulfur didn't appear
in the blood until then,

00:24:59.266 --> 00:25:01.566
So, no, there would be
no way of knowing.

00:25:01.599 --> 00:25:05.466
Not until
after duane...turns.

00:25:05.499 --> 00:25:09.000
Dean, i've got to talk
to you. Now.

00:25:11.165 --> 00:25:13.099
Sit in that chair
over there.

00:25:15.199 --> 00:25:19.032
This is my vision, dean.
It's happening.

00:25:19.065 --> 00:25:20.332
Yeah, i figured.

00:25:20.366 --> 00:25:21.799
You can't kill him.
Not yet.

00:25:21.833 --> 00:25:23.699
We don't know
if he's infected or not.

00:25:23.733 --> 00:25:25.199
I think
we're pretty damn sure.

00:25:25.232 --> 00:25:27.199
Guy shows up out of nowhere,
cut on his leg,

00:25:27.232 --> 00:25:28.533
His whole family
is infected.

00:25:28.566 --> 00:25:30.441
We should keep him tied up,
and we should wait and see.

00:25:30.441 --> 00:25:33.332
For him to hulk out,
infect somebody else?

00:25:33.366 --> 00:25:35.099
No, thanks.
Can't take that chance.

00:25:36.533 --> 00:25:38.266
Look, man.
I'm not happy about this,

00:25:38.299 --> 00:25:40.165
But it's a tough job,
and you know that.

00:25:40.199 --> 00:25:41.399
It's supposed to be tough.

00:25:41.432 --> 00:25:44.437
We're supposed to struggle
with this.

00:25:44.437 --> 00:25:44.498
What does that buy us?

00:25:44.499 --> 00:25:46.633
A clear conscience,
for one.

00:25:46.666 --> 00:25:47.733
It's too late for that.

00:25:47.766 --> 00:25:50.065
What the hell
has happened to you?

00:25:50.099 --> 00:25:53.533
You might kill an innocent man,
and you don't even care.

00:25:53.566 --> 00:25:55.332
You don't act
like yourself anymore.

00:25:55.366 --> 00:25:59.266
You're acting like
one of those things out there.

00:26:02.099 --> 00:26:03.366
Hey.

00:26:05.032 --> 00:26:06.666
Open the damn door.

00:26:06.699 --> 00:26:08.499
Dean!

00:26:08.533 --> 00:26:11.866
Don't do it, dean!
Don't!

00:26:21.199 --> 00:26:23.900
No, no, no, no.
No, you're not gonna --

00:26:23.933 --> 00:26:28.432
No, no, i swear!
It's not in me!

00:26:28.466 --> 00:26:30.266
Oh, god.
We're all gonna die.

00:26:30.299 --> 00:26:31.866
Maybe he's telling
the truth.

00:26:31.900 --> 00:26:34.499
No, he's not him --
Not anymore.

00:26:34.533 --> 00:26:38.900
Ask her! Ask the doctor!
It's not in me!

00:26:38.933 --> 00:26:41.466
I...just...

00:26:42.399 --> 00:26:43.566
i can't tell.

00:26:45.933 --> 00:26:47.933
Please, don't.

00:26:47.966 --> 00:26:50.766
Don't, please.
I swear it's not in me.

00:26:50.799 --> 00:26:56.875
It's not in me, i swear.
I swear, it's not in me.

00:26:57.199 --> 00:26:58.866
I've got no choice.

00:27:27.599 --> 00:27:29.165
Damn it.

00:27:55.232 --> 00:27:57.199
It's been
over four hours.

00:27:57.232 --> 00:27:58.699
Duane's blood
is still clean.

00:27:58.733 --> 00:28:01.199
I don't think
he's infected.

00:28:01.232 --> 00:28:04.232
I'd like to untie him,
if that's all right.

00:28:11.232 --> 00:28:13.866
Sure. Yeah.

00:28:19.966 --> 00:28:22.366
You know
i'm gonna ask you why.

00:28:22.399 --> 00:28:26.199
Yeah, i know.

00:28:26.232 --> 00:28:29.266
So, why?
Why didn't you do it?

00:28:33.332 --> 00:28:34.833
We need more alcohol.

00:28:41.533 --> 00:28:44.132
How are you holding up,
pam?

00:28:44.165 --> 00:28:47.833
Good.
It will all be over soon.

00:28:54.733 --> 00:28:58.833
In fact...

00:28:58.866 --> 00:29:01.332
i've been waiting
for this the whole time.

00:29:01.366 --> 00:29:02.666
For what?

00:29:02.699 --> 00:29:04.866
To get you alone.

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:06.165
Aah!

00:29:36.232 --> 00:29:38.032
She bled on him.

00:29:39.966 --> 00:29:42.032
He's got the virus.

00:29:57.235 --> 00:29:59.777
Doctor, check his wound again,
would you?

00:30:05.828 --> 00:30:08.158
What does she need to
examine him for?

00:30:08.158 --> 00:30:10.387
You saw what happened.

00:30:10.387 --> 00:30:12.376
Did her blood
actually enter your wound?

00:30:12.376 --> 00:30:13.574
Come on,
of course it did!

00:30:13.575 --> 00:30:16.642
We can't take a chance.
You know what we have to do.

00:30:16.676 --> 00:30:18.176
Nobody is shooting
my brother.

00:30:18.209 --> 00:30:20.442
He's not gonna be
your brother much longer.

00:30:20.475 --> 00:30:23.009
Nobody's shooting anyone.
You were gonna shoot me!

00:30:23.043 --> 00:30:24.709
I still might.

00:30:24.742 --> 00:30:26.343
Dean, they're right.
I'm infected.

00:30:26.376 --> 00:30:28.809
Just give me the gun,
and i'll do it myself.

00:30:28.842 --> 00:30:31.310
Dean, i'm not gonna
become one of those things.

00:30:31.343 --> 00:30:32.609
We've still
got some time.

00:30:32.642 --> 00:30:33.842
Time for what?

00:30:33.876 --> 00:30:36.109
I understand he's your brother,
and i'm sorry.

00:30:36.143 --> 00:30:37.275
But i've got to take care
of this.

00:30:37.275 --> 00:30:40.181
You make a move, you'll be dead
before you hit the ground.

00:30:40.181 --> 00:30:42.047
Do i make myself clear?

00:30:42.048 --> 00:30:43.281
What are we
supposed to do?!

00:30:53.314 --> 00:30:55.747
Get the hell out of here.
That's what.

00:30:56.747 --> 00:31:00.664
Take my car.
You've got the explosives.

00:31:00.664 --> 00:31:03.497
There's an arsenal in there.
You two go with him.

00:31:03.531 --> 00:31:05.264
You got enough firepower
to handle anything now.

00:31:05.264 --> 00:31:06.531
What about you?

00:31:08.698 --> 00:31:11.932
Sam: dean, no.

00:31:11.965 --> 00:31:13.632
No.

00:31:13.665 --> 00:31:15.798
Go with them.
This is your only chance.

00:31:15.832 --> 00:31:18.632
You're not gonna
get rid of me that easy.

00:31:18.665 --> 00:31:21.164
No, he's right, man.
Come with us.

00:31:28.832 --> 00:31:30.465
Okay, it's your funeral.

00:31:36.965 --> 00:31:40.965
I'm sorry. Thanks for
everything, marshals.

00:31:40.999 --> 00:31:43.798
Oh, actually,
we're not really marshals.

00:31:43.832 --> 00:31:47.231
Um...oh.

00:32:05.231 --> 00:32:07.865
I wish
we had a deck of cards

00:32:07.898 --> 00:32:09.865
Or a foosball table
or something.

00:32:12.465 --> 00:32:16.131
Dean, don't do this.

00:32:16.164 --> 00:32:19.865
Just get the hell out
of here.

00:32:19.898 --> 00:32:21.732
No way.

00:32:26.365 --> 00:32:29.832
Give me my gun and leave.

00:32:29.865 --> 00:32:35.665
For the last time,
sam, no.

00:32:39.198 --> 00:32:42.832
This is the dumbest thing
you've ever done.

00:32:42.865 --> 00:32:45.164
I don't know about that.

00:32:45.198 --> 00:32:48.498
Remember that waitress
in tampa?

00:32:50.465 --> 00:32:55.099
Dean, i'm sick.
It's over for me.

00:32:55.131 --> 00:32:57.598
It doesn't have to be
for you.

00:32:57.632 --> 00:32:59.565
No, you can keep going.

00:32:59.598 --> 00:33:01.832
Who says i want to?

00:33:02.932 --> 00:33:04.765
What?

00:33:14.465 --> 00:33:15.798
I'm tired, sam.

00:33:16.865 --> 00:33:19.798
I'm tired of this job...

00:33:19.832 --> 00:33:22.365
this life...

00:33:22.398 --> 00:33:24.665
this weight
on my shoulders, man.

00:33:24.698 --> 00:33:25.898
I'm tired of it.

00:33:25.932 --> 00:33:28.398
So, what?
So, you're just gonna give up?

00:33:28.431 --> 00:33:30.565
I mean, you're just
gonna lay down and die?

00:33:30.598 --> 00:33:32.965
Look, dean, i know this stuff
with dad had --

00:33:32.999 --> 00:33:34.898
You're wrong.

00:33:36.431 --> 00:33:39.732
It's not about dad.

00:33:39.765 --> 00:33:41.865
I mean,
part of it is, sure --

00:33:41.898 --> 00:33:43.765
Then, what is it about?

00:34:00.465 --> 00:34:01.732
You better
come see this.

00:34:21.331 --> 00:34:24.298
There's no one.
Not anywhere.

00:34:24.331 --> 00:34:28.365
They've all
just vanished.

00:34:41.965 --> 00:34:44.264
Well,
it's been five hours,

00:34:44.298 --> 00:34:46.099
And your blood's
still clean.

00:34:46.131 --> 00:34:48.498
I don't understand it,
but i think you dodged a bullet.

00:34:48.531 --> 00:34:51.865
But i was exposed.
How could i not be infected?

00:34:51.898 --> 00:34:54.498
I don't know,
but you're just not.

00:34:54.531 --> 00:34:57.898
I mean, when you compare it
with the tanner samples --

00:34:57.932 --> 00:34:58.932
What the hell?

00:34:58.965 --> 00:35:01.565
What?

00:35:01.598 --> 00:35:06.164
Their blood --
There's no trace of the virus.

00:35:06.198 --> 00:35:09.099
No sulfur. Nothing.

00:35:17.431 --> 00:35:20.732
The sarge and i are
getting the hell out of here.

00:35:20.765 --> 00:35:23.065
Heading south.
You should come.

00:35:23.099 --> 00:35:24.732
I'd better get over
to sidewinder,

00:35:24.765 --> 00:35:26.164
Get the authorities
up here.

00:35:26.198 --> 00:35:29.665
If they'll believe me.

00:35:29.698 --> 00:35:31.264
Take care.

00:35:32.598 --> 00:35:34.832
What about him?

00:35:34.865 --> 00:35:38.765
He's gonna be fine.
No signs of infection.

00:35:51.431 --> 00:35:55.398
Hey, man, don't look at me.
I've got no clue.

00:35:55.431 --> 00:35:57.565
I swear, i'm gonna lose sleep
over this one.

00:35:57.598 --> 00:35:59.231
I mean, why here?
Why now?

00:35:59.264 --> 00:36:00.832
Where the hell
did everybody go?

00:36:00.865 --> 00:36:02.765
It's not like
they just freaking melted.

00:36:02.798 --> 00:36:05.698
Why was i immune?

00:36:05.732 --> 00:36:08.565
Yeah, you know what?
That's a good question.

00:36:08.598 --> 00:36:10.398
You know, i'm already
starting to feel

00:36:10.431 --> 00:36:12.765
Like this is the one
that got away.

00:36:41.698 --> 00:36:46.798
Do you mind pulling over
up ahead there?

00:36:46.832 --> 00:36:48.365
All right.

00:36:55.932 --> 00:36:57.632
I've got to make a call.

00:36:57.665 --> 00:36:59.099
No phone out here.

00:36:59.131 --> 00:37:01.231
I got it covered.

00:37:01.264 --> 00:37:03.032
What the hell is that?

00:37:30.398 --> 00:37:33.498
It's over.
You'll be pleased.

00:37:33.531 --> 00:37:38.099
I don't think any more tests
are necessary.

00:37:38.131 --> 00:37:43.465
The winchester boy --
Definitely immune as expected.

00:37:43.498 --> 00:37:48.632
Yes, of course.
Nothing left behind.

00:38:20.208 --> 00:38:23.508
So, last night --
You want to tell me

00:38:23.542 --> 00:38:26.508
What the hell
you were talking about?

00:38:26.542 --> 00:38:27.842
What do you mean?

00:38:27.875 --> 00:38:29.076
What do i mean?

00:38:29.108 --> 00:38:31.554
I mean you said
you were tired of the job

00:38:31.554 --> 00:38:33.774
And that it wasn't
just because of dad.

00:38:33.774 --> 00:38:34.785
Forget it.

00:38:34.785 --> 00:38:36.751
No, i can't.
No way.

00:38:36.752 --> 00:38:38.219
I thought
we were both gonna die.

00:38:38.253 --> 00:38:39.586
You can't hold that
over me.

00:38:39.620 --> 00:38:41.286
You can't pull that crap
with me, man.

00:38:41.319 --> 00:38:42.286
You're talking.

00:38:42.319 --> 00:38:43.785
And what if i don't?

00:38:43.819 --> 00:38:46.785
Then i guess i'll just have to
keep asking you

00:38:46.819 --> 00:38:47.952
Till you do.

00:38:53.819 --> 00:38:55.952
I don't know, man.

00:38:55.986 --> 00:38:58.486
I just think
maybe we ought to...

00:39:01.486 --> 00:39:03.819
...go to the grand canyon.

00:39:05.819 --> 00:39:07.685
What?

00:39:07.719 --> 00:39:09.153
Yeah, you know,
all this driving

00:39:09.186 --> 00:39:10.785
Back and forth
across the country --

00:39:10.819 --> 00:39:12.952
Do you know i've never
been to the grand canyon?

00:39:12.986 --> 00:39:14.919
Or we could go to t.J.
Or hollywood --

00:39:14.952 --> 00:39:16.819
See if we could
bang lindsay lohan.

00:39:16.852 --> 00:39:18.752
You're not
making any sense.

00:39:18.785 --> 00:39:22.419
I just think we should
take a break from all this.

00:39:22.453 --> 00:39:24.919
Why do we got to get stuck
with all the responsibility?

00:39:24.952 --> 00:39:27.586
Why can't
we live life a little bit?

00:39:27.620 --> 00:39:29.319
Why are you
saying all this?

00:39:32.319 --> 00:39:34.119
No, no, no, no, no.

00:39:34.153 --> 00:39:36.785
Dean, you're my brother,
all right?

00:39:36.819 --> 00:39:39.419
So, whatever weight
you're carrying,

00:39:39.453 --> 00:39:40.919
Let me help
a little bit.

00:39:45.019 --> 00:39:48.319
I can't.
I promised.

00:39:48.353 --> 00:39:49.553
Who?

00:39:49.586 --> 00:39:51.752
Dad.

00:39:53.852 --> 00:39:56.286
What are you
talking about?

00:39:57.553 --> 00:40:03.019
Right before dad died...
he told me something.

00:40:05.286 --> 00:40:07.620
He told me something
about you.

00:40:10.719 --> 00:40:12.719
What?

00:40:14.886 --> 00:40:18.219
Dean,
what did he tell you?

